<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Amman</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Rabbath Ammon</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Amman is the capital and largest city of Jordan. As Rabbah, or Rabbath Ammon, it was the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iron-age">Iron Age</a> kingdom of Ammon; the Ptolemies refounded it as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philadelphia">Philadelphia</a>, and it became a city of the Decapolis with a Roman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theatre">theatre</a> that still stands. It was a small town when Abdullah made it the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">Emirate</a> of Transjordan in 1921, and it has grown with successive waves of refugees since 1948.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/amman.jpg" alt="Amman" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ramzik1999 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:New_Abdali_2024.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>After months of political crisis, including the assassination of southern politicians and a reconciliation accord signed in <b>Amman</b> in February 1994 that was never implemented, major clashes began in late April and became full-scale war in May.</blockquote><a href="/empire/republic-of-yemen">Republic of Yemen · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>After the Treaty of Paris of 1783 recognised independence, with a western border on the Mississippi, debts and unrest such as Shays' Rebellion of 1786–1787 persuaded leaders to call the Constitutional Convention at <b>Philadelphia</b> in 1787.</blockquote><a href="/empire/united-states">United States · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>The Ammonites formed a kingdom in the 10th century BCE or earlier, on the plateau around the upper Jabbok river, with its capital at <b>Rabbah</b>, the citadel of modern Amman.</blockquote><a href="/state/ammon">Ammon</a></li><li><blockquote>A federal parliament, joint army and common foreign policy were planned, and the capital was to alternate between Baghdad and <b>Amman</b>.</blockquote><a href="/state/arab-federation">Arab Federation</a></li><li><blockquote>The Decapolis cities, among them Gerasa, Gadara, Pella, <b>Philadelphia</b>, Scythopolis and Hippos, had grown as Greek-style towns under the Ptolemaic Empire and the Seleucid Empire.</blockquote><a href="/state/decapolis-levant">Decapolis (Levant)</a></li><li><blockquote>Abdullah built a state from Bedouin tribes and small towns, making <b>Amman</b> his capital.</blockquote><a href="/state/emirate-of-transjordan">Emirate of Transjordan</a></li></ul></section>
